Package: tidypm
Title: Tidy Tools for Multi-Asset Portfolio Management
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sebastian", "Stöckl", email = "sebastian.stoeckl@uni.li",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2984-1462")))
Description: Tools for multi-asset portfolio management that stand beside
    'PortfolioAnalytics' rather than wrapping it. Included are a tibble
    interface to the wide return matrices it expects, reproducible access to
    public data through a pinned cutoff date and a local cache, portfolio
    universes and screens, total returns for constant-maturity government and
    credit bonds built from yields, a strategy register with an out-of-sample
    backtest that charges trading costs by asset class, and per-period
    diagnostics reporting which dates of a rolling optimization produced a
    portfolio and what went wrong at the others. A simulated multi-asset market
    is shipped with the package so that every example runs offline. Companion
    package to the book "Tidy Asset Allocation in R".
